---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config } from "../../config";
import { privacyLine } from "../../data/features";
---
<Legal title="Privacy notice" description="How olá collects, uses and protects personal data.">
  <p><strong>In short:</strong> {privacyLine}</p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {config.companyName} is the controller of your personal data. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data</strong> (name, email, password hash, country) — to provide your account. Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Order data</strong> (items, amounts, shipping address, tracking) — to deliver your order and meet tax and accounting duties. Legal basis: contract and legal obligation.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment and billing data</strong> — payments are handled by Stripe; we do not store your full card details.
      When you agree at checkout that we may charge your saved card for <Brand name="care" />, we keep a record of that
      agreement, including the IP address and browser details recorded at the time. Legal basis: contract, legal
      obligation, and our legitimate interests in being able to show that you agreed to recurring billing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Voice</strong> — the watch sends audio only after you press the top button or tap the mic. Our server passes
      it to our AI provider, OpenAI, to turn it into text. We do not store recordings of your voice on our servers.
      Legal basis: contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Conversations</strong> — the text of what you said and olá's replies. Replies are written by OpenAI's
      language models and turned into speech by OpenAI. Transcripts and replies are stored in your conversation history.
      Legal basis: contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Long-term memory</strong> — memory is on by default. olá can remember facts when you ask it to (for example
      “remember that…”) and can learn facts from your conversations, so that its answers suit you. You can switch memory
      off on the Memory page of your account, forget single items, or forget everything. Sensitive information, such as
      details about your health, religion or political views, is kept only if you explicitly ask olá to remember it.
      Legal basis: contract; for sensitive information, your explicit consent, which you can withdraw by deleting it.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Notes and reminders</strong> you create with olá or in your account. Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Web search</strong> — for questions about current events, olá searches the web. The search question,
      never your name or account details, is sent to a search service (OpenAI's hosted web search, or Brave Search,
      DuckDuckGo and Yahoo), and olá may then read the most relevant public web pages. For weather, the town you ask
      about is sent to MET Norway and OpenStreetMap's Nominatim service to find its forecast. Your approximate city,
      worked out from your watch's time zone, may be included so results are relevant. Some general answers (for example weather, transport, sport, business and news) may be stored for a short time and
      reused for other users' similar questions; these stored answers do not identify you. Legal basis: contract.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Watch settings and usage</strong> (language, persona, colours, the number of AI interactions used in each billing period). Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Diagnostics</strong> — technical records about the watch and the service, such as errors and incidents.
      They do not contain the content of your conversations. Legal basis: legitimate interests (keeping the service
      working and secure).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Application logs</strong> — operational records our servers keep to run the service and protect it. We are
      working to remove personal content from them. Legal basis: legitimate interests (security and operations).
    </li>
    <li><strong>Website analytics</strong> — {config.plausibleDomain ? "cookieless, aggregated statistics (Plausible); no personal profiles." : "none at present."} Legal basis: legitimate interests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We use these service providers, who process data on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>OpenAI — speech-to-text, AI replies, text-to-speech and web search.</li>
    <li>Stripe — payments and billing.</li>
    <li>Our email delivery provider — account and service emails.</li>
    <li>Our hosting provider — the servers that run olá.</li>
    <li>Delivery carriers — name, address and contact details needed to deliver your order.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To answer web questions, the search question (or, for weather, the town) is also sent to independent search and
    data services: Brave Search, DuckDuckGo, Yahoo, MET Norway and OpenStreetMap (Nominatim). They receive it from our
    servers, not from your watch, and never with your name or account details.
  </p>
  <p>We never sell your data and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers may process data outside the UK, for example OpenAI in the United States. Where your data is
    transferred outside the UK, we use safeguards recognised under UK data protection law, such as the International
    Data Transfer Agreement or the UK Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, or rely on UK adequacy
    regulations where they apply.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Conversation history</strong> (transcripts and replies): until you delete it or your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Memories</strong>: until you forget them (one by one or all at once) or delete your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Notes and reminders</strong>: until you delete them or your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Voice recordings</strong>: not stored on our servers.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stored web search answers</strong>: general answers that don't identify you expire after a short time.
      Answers linked to your account also expire, and are deleted with your account.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Diagnostics and incident records</strong>: 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Application logs</strong>: for a limited period, for security and operations.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Backups</strong>: we take daily backups of our database and keep them for 14 days. Data you delete may stay in
      these backups until they expire, for up to 14 days. Where we keep encrypted off-site copies, these expire after 30 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Order, payment and billing records</strong>, including the record of your agreement to recurring billing: as
      long as the law requires for tax and accounting (typically 6–10 years), and as long as we need them to show that you
      agreed.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Usage counts</strong> (how many interactions were used, without any content): as long as we need them for billing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>When you delete your account in your olá account settings, we:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>delete your profile, conversation history, memories, notes and reminders, and personas;</li>
    <li>unpair your watches;</li>
    <li>
      cancel any <Brand name="care" /> subscription straight away in Stripe, so you won't be charged again. There is no
      automatic refund for the current period.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We keep order, payment and billing-consent records (including the IP address and browser details recorded when you
    agreed to recurring billing) as required for tax and accounting and to show that you agreed, and usage counts without
    any content for billing. Deleted data may remain in our backups until they expire, as described above.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected, to have it erased, to restrict or object to certain
    processing, to receive your data in a portable format, and to withdraw your consent where we rely on consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    Many of these you can do yourself in your account: download a copy of your data, delete your conversation history,
    manage or switch off memory, and delete your account. For anything else, email
    <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a>. We respond within one month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office
    (<a href="https://ico.org.uk/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, 0303 123 1113). If you live in the EU, you can also
    contact your local data protection authority. We'd appreciate the chance to put things right first.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>olá is intended for adults. You must be 18 or over to buy an <Brand name="watch" /> and create an account.</p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Your olá account and our website are served over encrypted (HTTPS) connections, and our servers reach our AI
    provider over encrypted connections. Your conversations are not end-to-end encrypted: our servers and OpenAI process
    them so that olá can answer you. Access to personal data is restricted to people who need it. See
    <a href="/security/">Security</a> to report a vulnerability.
  </p>
</Legal>
